Softmax turns logits zi into probabilities. Temperature T divides the logits first:
pi=ezi/T∑jezj/T
T<1 sharpens the distribution, T>1 flattens it, and as T approaches 0 sampling approaches greedy decoding (always the top token). Watch it with made-up logits for the word after "The cat sat on the":
# sampling_toy.py
import numpy as np
words = np.array(["mat", "rug", "sofa", "floor", "moon"])
logits = np.array([3.0, 2.2, 1.5, 1.0, -1.0])
def softmax(z, temperature=1.0):
z = z / temperature
e = np.exp(z - z.max()) # subtract the max so exp() cannot overflow
return e / e.sum()
rng = np.random.default_rng(42)
for t in (0.2, 0.7, 1.0, 1.5):
p = softmax(logits, t)
picks = rng.choice(words, size=1000, p=p)
counts = {str(w): int((picks == w).sum()) for w in words}
print(f"T={t:<4} p={np.round(p, 2)} {counts}")
